## Final single-owner deployment transaction

PR #125 merged as `e4cf04ab63966e9002e3403eff64fffda8d8d757` after exact-head validation:

- Shared Files Guard `29907160633`: success;
- Editorial Metadata v3 `29907160694`: success.

The permanent topology now has one automatic production entry point:

1. every `main` push enters **Metadata & IndexNow Readiness** (`**` catch-all plus documented critical path classes);
2. Pages runs only from a successful readiness `workflow_run` restricted to `main`;
3. automatic deploy checks out the exact `workflow_run.head_sha`, not moving `main`;
4. direct `deploy.on.push` is forbidden by permanent regression tests;
5. manual `workflow_dispatch` recovery remains available.

Keeping #58 open until the observer records one successful Pages run for `e4cf04ab` and PASS for all five critical production blob comparisons.

## Deploy topology correction merged

PR #125 was squash-merged as `e4cf04ab63966e9002e3403eff64fffda8d8d757` after the exact candidate head passed Shared Files Guard and Editorial Metadata v3.

Permanent invariants now enforced:
- every automatic `main` push enters `Metadata & IndexNow Readiness` exactly once;
- `Deploy to GitHub Pages` has no direct `push` trigger;
- mixed source/asset commits cannot create competing Pages transactions;
- automatic deploy checks out the exact `github.event.workflow_run.head_sha` that passed readiness, not moving `main`;
- direct automatic push entry and moving-main checkout are blocked by regression tests.

Keeping #58 open until the observer records one successful readiness run, one successful Pages run for the same verified SHA, and PASS for all five source/production blob comparisons.
